### Note on one small improvement in Step 5:
I moved `.setNumberFormat('@')` **above** `.setValues(finalGrid)`. In Google Sheets, if you write `"2021-04-03 09:12"` or `"2,3"` to an unformatted cell first, Sheets immediately converts it to a numeric date or number before formatting applies. Setting the plain-text format (`@`) *before* writing guarantees your ISO timestamp strings and `SourceRows` stay exact text strings.

